2. THE ONLY CONDITION: ATTRIBUTION

The rights granted above are conditioned on a single requirement: every
Product must visibly credit the Ruzit engine.

  (a) The credit must include the word "Ruzit" and make clear that the
      Product was made with, built on, or powered by the Ruzit engine.
      Wording such as "Made with Ruzit", "Powered by Ruzit", or "Built
      with the Ruzit engine" satisfies this requirement.

  (b) The credit may appear in any one reasonable, human-readable
      location that an ordinary user of the Product can find, including
      but not limited to: a credits screen or credits list, an "About"
      screen or dialog, the title or splash screen, an end-of-game
      credits roll, documentation, a settings/info menu, or an
      accompanying readme or license file shipped with the Product. You
      are not required to display it in more than one place.

  (c) The credit must be in a legible form and must not be hidden,
      obfuscated, or made deliberately difficult to find.

  (d) You may modify the engine and change anything about it; a modified
      version of the Software is still the Software for the purpose of
      this Section, and Products built on a modified version must still
      carry the Ruzit credit.

No other condition applies. You do not need to ask permission, register,
report your usage, or pay anything.


3. INDEPENDENT AND CLEAN-ROOM WORKS

The attribution requirement in Section 2 applies only to Products that
actually include, embed, or run on the Software. It does not apply to an
independent work that you create by studying, learning from, or being
inspired by the Software, as long as that independent work does not copy
or incorporate the Software's own code, assets, or files.

In plain terms: if you build your own engine or tools by studying how
Ruzit works, that independent engine is entirely yours, owes no credit
under this license, and is in no way restricted by it.


